jros2: a history lookup finds a change when another writer's change has the same source timestamp

History::find_change_nts() searched with std::lower_bound and history_order_cmp, and accepted only the change the
binary search landed on. history_order_cmp orders the changes of different writers by source timestamp only, so when a
change of another writer with exactly the same timestamp came first in the history, the search stopped on that change
and reported the change as missing although it was there. Equal timestamps are common with coarse clocks (1 us on
macOS, 100 ns on Windows) when several writers of one process publish at the same instant.

DataReaderHistory::remove_change_sub() then left a sample that take() had returned in the reader history, and
ReadTakeCommand::add_instance(), which ignores the result, returned that same sample on every later take. A listener
that takes until no data is left (jros2) kept taking it, holding the reader's lock and, with intraprocess delivery,
blocking every writer of the process that writes to that reader. The same miss could make a full KEEP_LAST reader
reject a new sample, after taking its oldest sample out of the instance but not out of the history.

When the change the binary search lands on is not the one searched for, the lookup now searches the whole history.

--- a/src/cpp/rtps/history/History.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/rtps/history/History.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <rtps/history/BasicPayloadPool.hpp>
 #include <rtps/history/CacheChangePool.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <mutex>
 
 namespace eprosima {
@@ -63,7 +64,12 @@
         return lb;
     }
 
-    return changesEnd();
+    // history_order_cmp orders the changes of different writers by source timestamp only, so when a change of another
+    // writer with the same timestamp comes first, the binary search stops on that change: search the whole history.
+    return std::find_if(changesBegin(), changesEnd(), [this, ch](const CacheChange_t* inner)
+                   {
+                       return matches_change(inner, ch);
+                   });
 }
 
